# S0b (STOP): the BAKED serving profile of the window image (the Lever N traffic profile) on the window image WITHOUT the audits: the bytes a platform launch serves. The smoke action always passes QWEN_C2_PROFILE, so the profile
# is named here; that the image boots it by its own default with no profile set is read in SR10 (the replay sets none). READ: '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic', admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED and no waiver,
# parser M armed; every hash EQUAL to S0-CTL's of W-1 and so to the production reference (the 32k prompts are split steps here: that the split prefill is exact is what A1-LN, P1ab-LN and E1-LN of W-1 proved). Measured basis: v579 8.9 minutes, v524 11.6.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-2 window pack (tp4-w2-levern-jobs: Lever N robustness, then the cutover; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stage1-windows and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the combined branch's engine with the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its
# default); a job that names tp4-serve-10 runs the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal
C2_BOX_MINUTES=20
